# --- The tool/content split (#20) ----------------------------------------
#
# The tool clones into .planning/ and is gitignored by the project that uses
# it. User content lives in planning-content/ and output in docs/plan/ — both
# committed. This repo must be able to improve without a user losing or
# rewriting their project documents.
#
# .planning/ keeps its own remote; that remote is the update channel (#51).
# Being ignored here is what stops it becoming a nested-repo problem.
#
# ⚠️ This line is INERT in this repo — this repo *is* the tool (#69), so there
# is no .planning/ here to ignore. The line that does real work is the one the
# setup script appends to the CONSUMER's .gitignore (#71). Keep this one
# anyway: it costs nothing and it is correct the moment anyone clones the tool
# inside this checkout.
.planning/

# --- Node / Next.js -------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Sandbox tier 3 (#56) is the one place the agent holds credentials. Nothing
# about that should ever be committable by accident.
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
*.pem

# --- Agent-local settings -------------------------------------------------
#
# Per-machine tool permissions, not project configuration. It was ignored here
# only by a machine-global excludes file, which is not a property of the repo:
# on anyone else's clone it would have been offered up for commit.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- OS -------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
